### Create a CHED in the simulator, then validate it.
#
# The control API has no read-back endpoint by design — the SOAP face is the only way to read state,
# so the two cannot drift. The last request here reads the result back through trade-traces-poc,
# which is the easiest way to see what you built. For raw SOAP, use the Postman collection: the
# WS-Security PasswordDigest has to be computed per request and a .http file cannot do that.
#
# @simulator is the stub's control API — port 3000 in trade-gateway-local-environment, where 8085 is
# the publisher and will answer a control request with a bare 404. Running the stub on its own
# (docker compose up in this repo, or dotnet run) it is on 8085 instead.

@simulator = http://localhost:3000
@poc = http://localhost:8090
@chedId = CHEDA.XI.2026.0000005

### 1. Create.
#
# You state everything a submitter states. The simulator adds only what TRACES adds — display names,
# registry lookups, schema scaffolding — so this request is the certificate. CHED_TYPE is the one
# field it cannot be built without.

# @name create
POST {{simulator}}/control/cheds
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "NEW",

  "exchangedDocument": {
    "includedNote": { "CHED_TYPE": "A" },
    "declaration": {
      "actualDateTime": "2026-04-21T11:00:00+01:00",
      "includedClause": {
        "PURPOSE": "FREE_CIRCULATION",
        "GOODS_CERTIFIED_AS": "FATTENING"
      }
    }
  },

  "specifiedConsignment": {
    "availabilityDueDateTime": "2026-04-23T00:00:00+01:00",
    "exportCountry": "AF",
    "importCountry": "XI",

    "consignorParty": {
      "identifier": "770198",
      "postalAddress": { "countryId": "XI", "cityName": "Belfast" }
    },
    "consigneeParty": {
      "identifier": "899361",
      "postalAddress": { "countryId": "XI", "cityName": "Belfast" }
    },

    "unloadingBaseportLocation": { "identifier": "GBBEL", "countryId": "XI" },
    "mainCarriageLogisticsTransportMovement": {
      "modeCode": "3",
      "identifier": "GH 2357",
      "schemeId": "road_vehicle_registration_before_bcp"
    },

    "includedConsignmentItem": {
      "natureIdCargo": "12",
      "consignmentTotals": {
        "grossWeight": { "value": 50, "unitCode": "KGM" },
        "physicalReferencedLogisticsPackage": { "typeCode": "NA", "itemQuantity": 0 }
      },
      "includedTradeLineItem": [
        {
          "applicableClassification": { "CN": "0101" },
          "originCountry": "AF",
          "scientificName": "Bison",
          "netWeight": { "value": 900, "unitCode": "KGM" },
          "physicalReferencedLogisticsPackage": { "typeCode": "BX", "itemQuantity": 1 }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}

### 2. Validate it.
#
# A decision is a PATCH, not a resubmission. Notes and clauses are objects keyed by their code, so
# this merges into what is stored and the applicant's declaration above survives untouched.

# @name validate
PATCH {{simulator}}/control/cheds/{{chedId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "VALIDATED",
  "exchangedDocument": {
    "clearance": {
      "actualDateTime": "2026-04-23T10:00:00+01:00",
      "includedClause": {
        "DECISION_CONCLUSION": "ACCEPTABLE_FOR_FREE_CIRCULATION",
        "DOCUMENTARY_CHECK": "YES",
        "DOCUMENTARY_CHECK_RESULT": "SATISFACTORY",
        "IDENTITY_CHECK": "YES",
        "IDENTITY_CHECK_RESULT": "SATISFACTORY",
        "PHYSICAL_CHECK": "YES",
        "PHYSICAL_CHECK_RESULT": "SATISFACTORY"
      }
    }
  }
}

### 3. Read it back.
#
# Needs trade-traces-poc running, pointed at the simulator. Expect status "Issued (Validated)", the
# consignor named from the operator registry, and every clause carrying the display text beside its
# code — none of which was in the two requests above.

# @name read
GET {{poc}}/simulator/ched/{{chedId}}
Accept: application/json

### The same thing in a browser, rendered.

GET {{poc}}/simulator/ched/{{chedId}}?format=html

### Amend one check result, without restating the decision.

# @name amend
PATCH {{simulator}}/control/cheds/{{chedId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "exchangedDocument": {
    "clearance": {
      "includedClause": { "PHYSICAL_CHECK_RESULT": "NOT_SATISFACTORY" }
    }
  }
}

### Tidy up.

DELETE {{simulator}}/control/cheds/{{chedId}}
